# Rust Patterns — hyper-cdc-orchestrator

## Module layout

Modules are declared flat in `main.rs` (binary-local). Only `persist` and `function_runtime` live in `lib.rs` for reuse by the `cdc-processor` binary. Follow the same pattern for new modules.

```
src/
  main.rs      ← mod declarations, AppState, router wiring
  handlers.rs  ← HTTP handlers (thin)
  models.rs    ← shared DTOs / domain types
  reconcile.rs ← connector lifecycle domain logic
  my_new.rs    ← new domain module (declare: `mod my_new;` in main.rs)
```

## Naming conventions

- Modules: `snake_case` (e.g. `trigger_cdc`, `connector_catalog`)
- Response structs: `<Noun>Response` (e.g. `EngineStatusResponse`)
- Request structs: `<Noun>Request` or `<Noun>Params`
- Env vars: `ORCH_<NAME>` prefix

## Error handling

In **main crate** (`src/`): return `Result<T, AppError>`. Map external errors to the right variant:

```rust
// ✅ Good
fn call_connect(url: &str) -> Result<Value, AppError> {
    let res = client.get(url).send().await
        .map_err(|e| AppError::Upstream(e.to_string()))?;
    Ok(res.json().await.map_err(|e| AppError::Internal(e.to_string()))?)
}

// ❌ Bad — don't add anyhow to main crate
use anyhow::Result;  // only in mcp/ crate
```

In **mcp crate** (`mcp/src/`): use `anyhow::Result` and `thiserror::Error` — that crate already depends on them.

## Tracing

Instrument long-running or domain-critical async functions:

```rust
#[tracing::instrument(skip(state), fields(profile_id = %id))]
pub async fn reconcile_start(state: &AppState, profile: &mut CdcProfile) -> Result<(), AppError> {
    // ...
}
```

Use `tracing::info!`, `tracing::warn!`, `tracing::error!` — not `println!` or `eprintln!`.

## No `unwrap()` in production paths

```rust
// ❌ Bad
let val = map.get("key").unwrap();

// ✅ Good
let val = map.get("key")
    .ok_or_else(|| AppError::NotFound("key not found".into()))?;
```

`unwrap()` is acceptable only in unit tests and `#[cfg(test)]` blocks.

## Shared state access

`AppState` fields wrapped in `Arc<RwLock<…>>` require explicit lock:

```rust
// Read
let snapshots = state.connector_snapshots.read().await;

// Write — hold as briefly as possible
{
    let mut history = state.history.write().await;
    history.push(entry);
}
```

## Secret safety

Always call `profile.redact_secrets()` before serializing a profile into any HTTP response.

## Unit tests

Co-locate unit tests in the same file:

```rust
#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;

    #[tokio::test]
    async fn test_my_fn() {
        // ...
    }
}
```

API/integration tests live in `tests/api/all-apis.spec.ts` (Playwright).
